WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.196 --> 00:00:01.029
- All right, everybody.

00:00:01.029 --> 00:00:02.208
This hour is almost up,

00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:04.290
but I wanna share one
last gem on social media

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.250
that you may have missed.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.258
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.258 --> 00:00:09.678
(rock music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.678 --> 00:00:11.513
I know a lot of grownups
who reward themselves

00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:12.710
with a caramel macchiato

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.090
or a java chip frap from time to time,

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.650
but it's not just grownups obsessed

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.540
with such fancy and fun drinks.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.920
Kids are all about it as well.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.270
And that's why a Pittsburgh teacher

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.880
used her third grader's
love of one coffee chain

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.530
as a reward in the classroom.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.020
No, she did not just
completely dope them up

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.640
and pump them up full of caffeine.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.620
She put on a Starbucks incentive day,

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.930
transforming the classroom
into a coffee house

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.930
while slyly dropping
lessons into the recipe.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.310
We have her on the line right now.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.060
Everybody say hello to Taylor
watching on WTAE Channel 4.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.286
What's up, Taylor?

00:00:43.286 --> 00:00:44.762
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:45.595
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:45.595 --> 00:00:46.428
How are you?

00:00:46.428 --> 00:00:48.930
- First of all, thank you
so much for being a teacher.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.921
We love you for that.
(Kelly and audience clapping)

00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:52.341
- Thanks for having me.

00:00:52.341 --> 00:00:53.989
Thank you, that's amazing.
- Incredible,

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:54.840
incredible vocation.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.790
So, explain the incentive day.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.623
- Sure.

00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:00.060
So, almost every month I have some sort

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.940
of positive behavior incentive
for my third graders.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.760
I've done things like a
beach day, a camping day.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.870
Now, my class this year,

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.150
because they're huge fans,
they actually asked me

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.680
for the Starbucks day.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.020
And I said once they had
15 days of great behavior,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.860
we would have this.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.386
Now, I think just in about
15 days, they earned it.

00:01:17.386 --> 00:01:19.410
So, of course, I had to go all out.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.070
I decorated our entire classroom
with the green tablecloths.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:26.970
I had actual coffee cups
and treat bags for them.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.560
I myself wore a green apron.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.560
I played coffee house jazz
music throughout the day.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.240
And, of course, had to sprinkle in

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.280
a few educational components.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.660
So, some examples.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.950
We corrected the spelling

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.560
and grammatical errors
in a fictional menu,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.250
and we did some math by making
change with fictional orders.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.520
However, their favorite part,
as well as my favorite part,

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.200
were our coffee breaks throughout the day.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.260
Now, I didn't have actual
coffee served to them.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.520
I did have chocolate milk,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.040
but just like at the actual
Starbucks, they came up,

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.210
I wrote their name on their cup.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.760
I took their order with the
whipped creams and syrups

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.970
and called their names
and it was just a blast.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:03.990
- Very cool, man.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.117
Thank you so much for being
such an incredible teacher

00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:08.322
and also for joining us today.

00:02:08.322 --> 00:02:09.480
(audience clapping)

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.183
I'm liking your post right
now, Taylor, all right.

00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:13.410
- [Taylor] Thank you.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.243
- And that's not all.

00:02:14.243 --> 00:02:15.810
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.610
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.660
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.450
want to celebrate incredible
teachers just like you,

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.660
so they're giving the Hempfield
Area School District $1,000.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.790
How's that sound?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.407
(audience clapping)
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:27.407 --> 00:02:28.637
Thank you so much.

00:02:28.637 --> 00:02:29.850
- Thank you so much Taylor.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.757
Have such a blessed day.

00:02:30.757 --> 00:02:32.775
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:32.775 --> 00:02:35.579
Jenna Bush Hager, Barbara
Bush, Cailee Spaeny,

00:02:35.579 --> 00:02:37.439
Tiffany, and Daniel Carter.

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:38.272
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:38.272 --> 00:02:40.022
and if it's not, try and change it.

